        body: ['Language records human distinctions, activities and ways of describing the world. NLP turns that record into a representation and uses the representation for a task. The choice of representation decides what questions remain answerable.', 'A causal language model repeatedly predicts a distribution over the next token, selects a token, and extends the sequence. The tokenizer determines the units; training learns relationships among those units. A tiny hand-written probability table can demonstrate the loop, but it is a teaching model rather than a trained language model.', 'The course connects linguistic relativity to spatial reference: a language using cardinal directions can encourage different habits of orientation. Such examples motivate language as behavioral evidence; they do not mean word counts alone explain cognition.'],
        formula: 'text so far → next-token probabilities → selected token → extended text',
