        body: ['Tokenization selects units. Later preprocessing can lowercase them, remove punctuation or stopwords, and map word forms to lemmas. Lemmatization can turn heroes into hero and were into be. Each operation changes what the later model can see.', 'Keeping capitals can distinguish a company from a fruit. Keeping stopwords can preserve negation, style or grammatical context. Removing a stopword also changes the denominator in relative-frequency calculations even when the target word was never removed.', 'Retain the raw text, write down the complete pipeline and inspect examples before accepting a large table. The course uses spaCy for word-like analysis and compares it with the o200k_base subword tokenizer. A browser demonstration using a stated simple rule is not an implementation of either library.'],
        terms: 'Stopwords: common function words selected for removal. Lemma: a dictionary base form. Normalization: mapping multiple observed forms into one representation.',
