        formula: 'bigram model: P(wₜ | wₜ₋₁)     trigram model: P(wₜ | wₜ₋₂, wₜ₋₁)',
        example: '“the dog chased the ball” and “the ball chased the dog” have the same unigram counts. Their bigrams differ, exposing the change in local order.',
